+/// Effective memory bandwidth in GB/s for the device that will hold the
+/// weights, falling back to the measured system figure for integrated GPUs.
+///
+/// [`gpu_memory_bandwidth_gbps`] is a name lookup over discrete cards and the
+/// Strix Halo APUs. An ordinary mobile iGPU ("Radeon 840M / 860M Graphics",
+/// "Radeon 780M", Intel Iris/UHD) is in neither list, so it returns `None` and
+/// the caller drops to a run-mode constant calibrated on discrete GPUs — which
+/// on this class of hardware is wrong by several times, because an iGPU has no
+/// memory of its own. It streams weights from the same DDR as the CPU, over the
+/// same controller, so the system figure llmfit already measures *is* its
+/// bandwidth.
+///
+/// Measured on a Ryzen AI 7 PRO 350 / Radeon 860M (Krackan, RDNA 3.5):
+///   CPU, multithreaded memcpy (llmfit's own probe)   34 GB/s
+///   CPU, read-only stream (saturates at 4 threads)   34 GB/s
+///   iGPU, clpeak global memory bandwidth, rusticl    35.5 GB/s
+/// The GPU has no bandwidth advantage over the CPU here; both are limited by
+/// the same controller, not by their own path to it. Against that, the
+/// discrete-GPU constant had a dense 8B Q8 (8.2 GB of weights) at 16.1 tok/s,
+/// which would need ~130 GB/s.
+///
+/// Discrete cards missing from the table keep returning `None`: their VRAM
+/// bandwidth has no relationship to system DDR, so the old fallback is still
+/// the better guess there.
+pub fn effective_memory_bandwidth_gbps(name: &str, efficiency: f64) -> Option<f64> {
+    if let Some(bw) = gpu_memory_bandwidth_gbps(name) {
+        return Some(bw);
+    }
+    if SystemSpecs::is_integrated_gpu_name(name) && efficiency > 0.0 {
+        // The table stores spec-sheet peaks, which the caller derates by
+        // `efficiency`. The probe already reports an achieved figure, so
+        // returning it raw would derate twice. Pre-divide so the caller's
+        // multiply reconstructs the calibrated number, using the live config
+        // value rather than a hardcoded copy of its default.
+        return measured_read_bandwidth_gbps()
+            .map(|bw| bw * IGPU_DECODE_BANDWIDTH_FACTOR / efficiency);
+    }
+    None
+}
